nical specification (all ten protocols)"}]}],"id":"blk-96897","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161248","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-008-HARNESS"},{"id":"spn-161249","text":" — the Agent Harness Protocol specification"}]}],"id":"blk-96899","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161250","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-009-PRISM-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-161251","text":" — PRISM diagnostic benchmark protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-96901","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161252","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-010-PULSE-SPECIFICATION"},{"id":"spn-161253","text":" — PULSE loop manifest standard"}]}],"id":"blk-96903","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161254","marks":["bold"],"text":"spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION"},{"id":"spn-161255","text":" — empirical evaluation of topology-aware continual learning"}]}],"id":"blk-96905","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-96907","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-161256","text":"Documentation index"}]},{"id":"blk-96908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161257","text":"Linked index of every page in this set (renders on GitHub and in the docs atlas; the toctrees above drive the Sphinx build):"}]},{"id":"blk-96909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161258","marks":["bold"],"text":"Guides"}]},{"id":"blk-96910","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161259","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/quickstart.md"}],"text":"Quickstart"}]}],"id":"blk-96911","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161260","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/runtime-walkthrough.md"}],"text":"Runtime Walkthrough"}]}],"id":"blk-96913","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161261","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/positioning.md"}],"text":"Positioning — The Missing Constraint: Runtime Governance in the Agent Stack"}]}],"id":"blk-96915","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96918","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161262","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/competitive-landscape.md"}],"text":"Competitive Landscape — Agent Governance and Runtime Enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-96917","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96920","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161263","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/comparison-table.md"}],"text":"Comparison — OpenSentience vs. Alternatives"}]}],"id":"blk-96919","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161264","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ecosystem-overview.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem Overview — How the Protocols Connect"}]}],"id":"blk-96921","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96924","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161265","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/research.md"}],"text":"Research Overview"}]}],"id":"blk-96923","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96926","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161266","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/faq.md"}],"text":"FAQ"}]}],"id":"blk-96925","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96928","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161267","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/skills/SKILLS.md"}],"text":"Agent Skills"}]}],"id":"blk-96927","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-96929","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161268","marks":["bold"],"text":"Specifications"}]},{"id":"blk-96930","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96932","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161269","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"}],"text":"OS-011 — GRASP: Grounded Readings, Actions and State Protocol"}]}],"id":"blk-96931","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96934","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161270","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"}],"text":"OS-E001 — Empirical Evaluation of Topology-Aware Continual Learning"}]}],"id":"blk-96933","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-96935","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161271","marks":["bold"],"text":"UX & build prompts"}]},{"id":"blk-96936","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96938","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161272","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/docs/ux/user-stories-embodiment.md"}],"text":"Embodiment (body-browser + body-os) — User Stories"}]}],"id":"blk-96937","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-96940","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161273","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/opensentience.org/prompts/OS-008-BUILD.md"}],"text":"OS-008 Agent Harness Protocol — Implementation Build Prompt"}]}],"id":"blk-96939","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-96941","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-161274","text":"The Three Enforcement Layers"}]},{"id":"blk-96942","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161275","text":"OpenSentience provides three layers of runtime enforcement:"}]},{"id":"blk-96943","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"OS-008 Harness:   \"Has this agent followed the correct process?\"\n                   Pipeline ordering, quality gates, sprint contracts\n\nOS-006 Shim:      \"Is this agent allowed to do this?\"\n                   Permissions, lifecycle, autonomy levels\n\nOS-007 Security:  \"Is this agent under attack?\"\n                   Threat detection, identity verification, circuit breakers"},{"id":"blk-96944","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161276","text":"All three log to the same append-only audit trail, creating a unified compliance record from protocol to permission to pipeline."}]},{"id":"blk-96945","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-161277","text":"The Three-Protocol Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-96946","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161278","text":"Above the cognitive primitives, OpenSentience publishes three sibling protocols that together turn the [&] portfolio into a measurable, composable, accountable agent substrate:"}]},{"id":"blk-96947","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  PRISM (OS-009) — measures loops over time   diagnostic │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  PULSE (OS-010) — declares loops + signals    temporal  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  [&] Protocol     — composes capabilities     structural│\n└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-96949","spans":[{"id":"spn-161279","text":"Layer"}]},{"id":"blk-96950","spans":[{"id":"spn-161280","text":"Question"}]},{"id":"blk-96951","spans":[{"id":"spn-161281","text":"Artifact"}]}],"id":"blk-96948","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-96952","spans":[{"id":"spn-161282","text":"[&]"}]},{"id":"blk-96953","spans":[{"id":"spn-161283","text":"What can each agent do, and how do they compose?"}]},{"id":"blk-96954","spans":[{"id":"spn-161284","marks":["code"],"text":"*.ampersand.json"}]}],[{"id":"blk-96955","spans":[{"id":"spn-161285","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-96956","spans":[{"id":"spn-161286","text":"How do their processes cycle and signal each other?"}]},{"id":"blk-96957","spans":[{"id":"spn-161287","marks":["code"],"text":"*.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-161288","text":" (loop manifest)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-96958","spans":[{"id":"spn-161289","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-96959","spans":[{"id":"spn-161290","text":"How well do those cycles actually work over time?"}]},{"id":"blk-96960","spans":[{"id":"spn-161291","text":"Diagnostic reports + leaderboards"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-96961","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161292","text":"A loop is "},{"id":"spn-161293","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE-conforming"},{"id":"spn-161294","text":" if its manifest validates against "},{"id":"spn-161295","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-161296","text":" and its runtime passes the 12-test conformance suite. A system is "},{"id":"spn-161297","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM-evaluable"},{"id":"spn-161298","text":" automatically once it is PULSE-conforming — PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-161299","marks":["code"],"text":"compose"},{"id":"spn-161300","text":" phase reads the manifest, injects scenarios at the declared "},{"id":"spn-161301","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-161302","text":" boundary, and observes outcomes via the declared "},{"id":"spn-161303","marks":["code"],"text":"learn"},{"id":"spn-161304","text":" phase. Adoption order is typically [&] → PULSE → PRISM."}]},{"id":"blk-96962","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-161305","text":"Relationship to the [&] Ecosystem"}]},{"id":"blk-96963","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161306","text":"OpenSentience occupies the "},{"id":"spn-161307","marks":["bold"],"text":"governance and research layer"},{"id":"spn-161308","text":" of the [&] stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-96964","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"  [&] Protocol        — capability composition (what an agent CAN do)\n  OpenSentience       — governance + harness (what an agent MAY do, and how)\n  Graphonomous        — memory + learning (OS-001, OS-002, OS-004, OS-005)\n  AgenTroMatic        — deliberation (OS-003)\n  Delegatic           — policy authoring (feeds into OS-006 enforcement)\n  Agentelic           — agent manifests (consumed by OS-006 install)\n  FleetPrompt         — marketplace (agents enter governance on install)\n  SpecPrompt          — acceptance criteria (consumed by OS-008 quality gates)"},{"id":"blk-96965","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161309","text":"The governance shim wraps any OTP "},{"id":"spn-161310","marks":["code"],"text":"child_spec"},{"id":"spn-161311","text":". It does not replace the supervised process — it interposes permission checks, lifecycle management, autonomy control, pipeline enforcement, and audit logging around it."}]},{"id":"blk-96966","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-161312","text":"Founding Thesis"}]},{"id":"blk-96967","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161313","text":"OpenSentience exists because intelligence without governance is generation without accumulation. The ten protocols formalize what structured accumulation requires: memory that consolidates, routing that detects cycles, deliberation that resolves conflict, attention that prioritizes, resources that adapt, governance that enforces boundaries, security that detects threats, a harness that orchestrates the entire pipeline, "},{"id":"spn-161314","marks":["bold"],"text":"diagnostics that measure whether the loop actually learns"},{"id":"spn-161315","text":" (PRISM), and a "},{"id":"spn-161316","marks":["bold"],"text":"temporal manifest"},{"id":"spn-161317","text":" that lets every loop in the ecosystem declare how it cycles and signals (PULSE)."}]},{"id":"blk-96968","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-161318","text":"The shim is deliberately thin. Governance should cost less than 1% of the system it governs. PULSE is a manifest standard with no required runtime. PRISM runs as a separate benchmark engine that any system can opt into via its PULSE manifest."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera54646qlfji3kof2tcw6md354iqvgitltog74xklv7qtpnd7qht3a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}